{"name":"Uran Mica","hex":"#93b778","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mica","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of hydrous aluminosilicate minerals characterized by highly perfect cleavage, so that they readily separate into very thin leaves, more or less elastic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mica"}],"entries":[{"title":"Uran","blocks":[{"text":"Uran is a coastal node of Navi Mumbai in situated in South Navi Mumbai's Raigad district, Maharashtra in Konkan division. It lies east of Mumbai, across the Dharamtar Creek. Uran is primarily a fishing and agriculture village. The primary languages spoken are Agri and Koli, a dialect of Marathi-Konkani."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Uran_Nagav_beach.jpg/330px-Uran_Nagav_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uran"},{"title":"Mica","blocks":[{"text":"Micas are a group of silicate minerals whose outstanding physical characteristic is that individual mica crystals can easily be split into fragile elastic plates. This characteristic is described as perfect basal cleavage. Mica is common in igneous and metamorphic rock and is occasionally found as small flakes in sedimentary rock. It is particularly prominent in many granites, pegmatites, and schists, and \"books\" of mica several feet across have been found in some pegmatites."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Mica_%286911818878%29.jpg/330px-Mica_%286911818878%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mica"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Karanja_Village-Uran.jpg/500px-Karanja_Village-Uran.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Karanja_Village-Uran.jp